WEBVTT

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.490
What's wrong, Yumoto?

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:23.360
Big bro...

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:24.460
Were you in a fight?

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.440
I didn't hit them...

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:27.830
because you always tell me...

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:31.060
it's not good to hit friends...

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:33.840
They hit you, but you didn't fight back?

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.430
Good job, Yumoto.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:40.550
Big bro!

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:44.850
Listen, Yumoto. The moon is 
there, even during the day.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.480
Morning and night, it stands 
watch over you from the sky.

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:52.240
And me, too.

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:56.110
When you're suffering, when 
you're sad, look up at the sky.

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:58.420
The daytime moon and your big brother

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:00.990
are always watching over you.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:03.460
I understand, Big bro!

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:40.800
Brotherly Love

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:44.110
What?

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:46.060
Reading to kindergarteners?

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:47.520
Yeah!

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.100
With the student council studying abroad,

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:52.240
the teachers asked the Defense 
Club to do it instead!

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:53.010
Huh?

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:54.510
Our seats...

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:57.140
Someone's in our usual spot.

00:02:57.140 --> 00:02:59.560
Who cares if someone else sits there?

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:02.200
You know the saying. Home 
is where the heart is.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:03.960
Anyway, what's going on?

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:04.660
Who are they?

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:07.830
I heard we got some exchange 
students recently.

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:08.870
Maybe it's them?

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:09.900
Huh?

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.500
So what about the crowd?

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:18.550
<b>Beppu Brothers</b>

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:18.550
Overwhelming support from
 young female fans!!
And male fans too?!{left under title}

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:18.550
<b>Examining the Hot and Handsome
 Beppu Brother Idols!
Digging into this mysterious
 duo's personal lives......{right under title}</b>

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:18.550
<b>Beppu Haruhiko
Birthday: August 21st
Leo Blood Tpe AB
Interests: Bonsai
Favorite food: Rice balls
Hated food: Carrots{left bottom}</b>

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:18.550
<b>Beppu Akihiko: 
Birthday: August 21st
Leo Blood Type AB 
Hobby: Calligraphy
Favorite food: Rice balls
Hated food: Green peppers{right bottom}</b>

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:16.140
The detective I hired says 
they're the Beppu twins.

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:18.730
Very handsome, excellent grades.

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:20.580
They earned the title "eternal pretty boys"

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:23.440
in the Pretty Boy Contest the other day.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:27.220
And they already have a follower 
clique known as the "Beppu Apes."

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:30.940
Yeah, let's sit somewhere else.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:35.860
So, Yumoto. What was that about 
reading to kindergarteners?

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:38.820
You'll do it, En-chan-senpai?!

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:43.040
No, I don't think I could 
handle reading to little kids.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:45.030
It sounds like a nice idea, but...

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:48.470
It would be one thing if it were a 
co-ed event with a girls' high school.

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:51.250
I never volunteer my services 
without compensation.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:54.410
I believe that activities that spread love

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:56.850
are something the Defense Club 
should always take part in!

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:57.760
Why?!

00:03:57.760 --> 00:03:59.710
Why do you hesitate?

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:00.850
Why?

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:03.180
Why were <i>you</i> chosen?!

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:05.390
To be a child development volunteer...

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:08.600
Those shining smiles of local children...

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:09.920
Why?

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:11.560
Why is it not me?!

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:14.470
I think there's a crazy in our midst.

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:15.760
Um...

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:17.890
You're Katari-kun, right?

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.280
From the Speaking Poets Society...

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:20.630
Yes.

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:22.400
I am Katari Tagaru.

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:24.720
<b>Katari Tagaru</b>

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:25.960
Representative of the Binan High School 
association, the Speaking Poets Society.

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:30.330
Because! To enjoy something is to speak 
of it. In other words, to recite.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:31.950
Humans are speaking mammals.

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:34.000
I am the world's mouthpiece!

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:36.080
Yeah, he's a crazy.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:37.670
He called himself a representative,

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:40.850
but he's the Speaking Poets 
Society's only member.

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:44.720
Yeah, I feel my soul crying out to 
me, "Be somewhere else right now."

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:46.790
Well, Katari-kun. See you later.

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:48.720
What are you guys doing?

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:50.600
What about reading to the kindergartners?

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:52.150
Nothing!

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:54.180
The art of recitation is beyond them!

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:55.470
Nonsense!

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:57.160
Only I can handle it!

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:00.650
What are you trembling for?

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:02.320
Are you mad?

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:03.690
Stop it, Haru.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.740
I know that angry people are funny,

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.780
but if you tease them, they 
might take it out on you.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.570
You two...

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:12.490
You're the Beppu siblings 
everyone's talking about.

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:13.760
Yes.

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:15.670
I am Haruhiko, the younger.

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:16.960
Akihiko, the elder.

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:18.420
Together, we are...

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:19.360
The school's...

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:20.250
...idols...

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:21.670
...the Beppu Brothers!

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:24.230
Now, why are you...

00:05:24.230 --> 00:05:26.120
...mad at the Defense Club?

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:27.130
Because!

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:30.680
I say "no thank you" to any 
out-loud reading done by them!

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:32.520
Such an act requires expressiveness!

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:35.000
That's something only I can do!

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:36.730
I don't quite get it...

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:38.820
...but you <i>are</i> very funny!

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:42.320
He seems usable.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:45.430
This is our chance to crush 
the Defense Club into bit parts.

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:46.990
Crush them into bit parts?

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:48.860
Nice one.

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:53.330
Seriously, it's not happening.

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:56.200
I'm not reciting any folktales 
to kindergartners.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:57.540
Yeah, same.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:00.290
Reciting pillow talk to 
high school girls, maybe.

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:03.420
Sorry to repeat myself, 
but I don't work for free.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:05.780
We've been through this over and over again.

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:07.800
But I really want to do it!

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:11.760
Everyone, the volunteer spirit 
is the very foundation of love!

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:14.770
To give is, itself, love! 
Why won't you do it?!

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:17.020
'Cause it's a pain in the neck?

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:20.840
But folktales are surprisingly 
trendy, aren't they?

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:22.990
I always used to watch that anime,

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:24.780
<i>"Folktales From Japan".</i>

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:29.000
Well, <i>The Crane's Gift</i> and 
<i>Momotaro</i> and such aside,

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:32.740
there's The <i>Crying Red Ogre</i> and 
other obscure classics, I suppose.

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:36.030
And the story of <i>The Gold 
Axe and the Silver Axe</i>

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:39.400
contains good advice for those 
entering the world of investment.

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:42.750
"When a deal sounds too good, 
there's always a catch."

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:45.930
I think <i>Urashima Taro</i> is my favorite.

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:47.300
That Otohime, you know?

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:50.470
I'd go a summer-long romance with her!

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:53.030
I always liked <i>Jizo and the Hats</i>!

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:55.800
My brother and I used to 
play Jizo and the Hats!

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:56.680
"Play"?

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:59.170
It's a game we'd play on snowy 
days. We'd weave hats out of sedge.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:00.100
<b>Candy</b>

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:01.230
<b>Sweet Dumplings</b>

00:06:59.170 --> 00:07:03.680
Then I had to give them to the Jizo statues 
without trading them for snacks in town.

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:05.400
That's a game? Really?

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:10.190
My brother used fun games to 
teach me all kinds of things.

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:11.460
Really?

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:13.620
Gora-san is truly an inscrutible person.

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:15.510
The Jizo and the Hats game...

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:17.220
that really takes me back...

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:21.580
One day when it snowed, I 
was five years old, I think.

00:07:21.890 --> 00:07:23.320
Listen, Yumoto.

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:26.180
I'm heading out for work.

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:28.550
I want you to do something 
nice while I'm gone.

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:30.990
That's right.

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:34.760
Take these hats to the Jizo 
statues outside of town.

00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:37.760
Don't stray from the path no matter what.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:38.860
Got it?

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:40.730
Yeah, got it!

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:45.940
So I started for the Jizo statues, 
just like my bro told me...

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:48.610
But I ran into a trap!

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:49.150
A trap?

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:51.470
Hey, boy.

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:53.320
You've got some nice-looking hats there.

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:55.070
I'm selling steamed buns here.

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:56.530
Wanna trade?

00:07:57.630 --> 00:07:58.830
They look delicious!

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:00.490
Well? Want to trade?

00:08:00.490 --> 00:08:01.420
Yeah!

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:04.420
Yes! Let's eat...

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:07.600
Listen, Yumoto.

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:10.880
Don't stray from the path no matter what.

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:13.180
No, I shouldn't.

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:14.700
I can't accept this.

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:17.360
But I'll still give you the hat.

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:18.600
I'm sorry.

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:21.110
Wait, you gave him the hat?

00:08:21.110 --> 00:08:22.150
Yeah.

00:08:22.150 --> 00:08:24.510
But I didn't take the steamed bun.

00:08:24.510 --> 00:08:27.610
So what about the four other hats?

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:29.960
I gave them to the Jizo statues.

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:31.220
But...

00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:35.780
There were five Jizo statues, 
and I was missing one hat.

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:41.250
I didn't realize until then that 
that's why Bro gave me five.

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:38.760
Oh no! I don't have enough!

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:45.670
So I had to take off my own scarf 
and put it on the Jizo statue.

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:47.880
Just like in the story, right?

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:50.260
I'm sorry I don't have a hat for you...

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:55.460
Yumoto...

00:08:55.460 --> 00:08:56.800
You did a very good thing.

00:08:57.780 --> 00:08:58.840
Bro...

00:09:00.530 --> 00:09:02.840
Gora-san came to watch, huh?

00:09:02.840 --> 00:09:03.900
Yeah.

00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:07.340
Because the snow was falling 
so hard, and he got worried.

00:09:07.340 --> 00:09:10.070
Your brother sounds like a real worrywart.

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:12.900
Like a parent watching over a 
kid running their first errand.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:16.770
Gora-san's brotherly love for 
Yumoto-san is higher than the sky

00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:19.490
and deeper than the sea!

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:22.120
Anyway, I want to tell 
little kids those folktales

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:25.380
just like my brother did for me.

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:26.400
Yumoto...

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:28.970
So, what should we do?

00:09:28.970 --> 00:09:31.310
If Yumoto wants to do it that badly...

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:32.980
It's hard to refuse out of hand.

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:34.180
Even if I must work for free.

00:09:34.180 --> 00:09:38.390
Are you guys seriously leaning 
towards reading to the kids?

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:42.760
Big bro, what's wrong?

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:45.610
Yumoto, reading to others <i>is</i> love!

00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:46.920
Do it right.

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:54.650
Yeah! Bro, I'll do my best!

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:59.420
Yeah, we're definitely gonna end 
up reading to the kids, aren't we?

00:09:59.420 --> 00:10:00.660
Looks like it.

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:05.080
<b>Earth Defense Club

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:09.760
Unbelievable!

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:12.760
How could they go over my head 
and give it to the Defense Club?!

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:14.110
Illegal!

00:10:14.110 --> 00:10:16.510
All recitation opportunities 
should fall to me!

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:19.340
Look at that jealousy.

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:21.470
It's truly petty.

00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:23.960
But those flames of petty jealousy

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:26.250
that others can't understand...

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:28.840
...can soon become raging infernos.

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:30.440
If we want to crush the Defense Club,

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:34.440
using Katari Tagaru is the best way.

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:35.690
The Defense Club...

00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:37.530
I don't like them.

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:39.380
Let's take 'em out.

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:44.870
<b>The Flashing Prince
Battle Lover Cerulean
Finishing Move: 
Cerulean Love Aqua</b>

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:49.140
What?

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:53.000
Just what are they planning to 
read to those kindergartners?

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:54.320
When...

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.870
The moment any one of 
them flubs even slightly,

00:10:56.870 --> 00:11:00.680
I shall mercilessly hijack their performance!

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:05.790
I really think I want to do the story 
of <i>Jizo and the Hats</i> for the kids.

00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:06.640
What do you think?

00:11:07.050 --> 00:11:09.050
It doesn't really matter to me.

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:13.110
I also have no objection, aside 
from the lack of compensation.

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:15.070
This reminded me.

00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:18.830
It's because my brother read 
folktales to me every night

00:11:18.830 --> 00:11:22.200
that I never felt lonely as a child.

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:25.530
Your parents have been gone that long?

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:30.540
Yeah! Bro says they're busy 
with their hot springs tour.

00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:32.860
That seems a bit suspect.

00:11:32.860 --> 00:11:35.210
Well, I guess everyone 
has their circumstances.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:40.170
Does that mean Gora-san's been 
your caretaker in every respect?

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:41.280
Yeah!

00:11:41.280 --> 00:11:45.080
From feeding me to brushing my 
teeth, my brother did it all!

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:49.390
My brother's lap was so warm...

00:11:50.420 --> 00:11:52.710
What is this feeling?

00:11:52.710 --> 00:11:54.350
It tugs at the heart strings, huh?

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:58.820
Because Gora-san looked after him even 
when he was still in high school himself!

00:11:59.130 --> 00:12:02.150
I brushed my own teeth, at least.

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:03.610
Even as a child.

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:07.160
Hey, didn't we forbid you from 
talking about tooth-brushing?

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:11.500
En-chan, there's no need to 
air out that old laundry.

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:18.090
Jesus!

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:22.420
The Defense Club has come 
together for the reading!

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:22.420
<b>Jizo and the Hats</b>

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:23.880
Nonsense!

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:27.100
Such work was meant for me!

00:12:27.410 --> 00:12:31.210
His flame of jealousy is 
burning even brighter.

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:37.020
You can't wage war on an empty stomach.

00:12:37.470 --> 00:12:39.740
Eat, Yumoto, along with your comrades!

00:12:39.740 --> 00:12:41.400
Thanks, Bro!

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:44.660
They're delicious, Bro!

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:48.330
But we're reading to kids. 
We're not waging war.

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:51.970
Life is an ongoing battle to 
convey one's love to others.

00:12:51.970 --> 00:12:53.860
Reading aloud to children

00:12:54.190 --> 00:12:56.960
is a battle to make those 
children feel loved.

00:12:57.240 --> 00:12:58.880
Got it, Bro!

00:12:59.180 --> 00:13:00.200
Look at him!

00:13:00.200 --> 00:13:03.130
Does he really think he's 
worthy to eat those riceballs?

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:05.840
Look at him, stuffing his face 
without a care in the world...

00:13:06.400 --> 00:13:07.760
It's unforgivable.

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:12.470
Flames of jealousy allow 
Galaxy Idols The VEPPer

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:14.360
to shine ever brighter.

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:22.820
<i>Jizo and the Hats</i> is about a 
poor yet kind elderly couple

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:25.370
who find Jizo statues on the 
roadside covered in snow,

00:13:25.370 --> 00:13:29.280
and give them the sedge hats they made to 
sell for money to them, expecting no reward.

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:30.300
Then, later,

00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:34.260
the Jizo statues come to return 
the favor in heartwarming fashion.

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:36.040
Difficult!

00:13:36.340 --> 00:13:38.760
There's no way the Defense 
Club could handle it!

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:40.200
That guy's creepy!

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:42.630
Shh! He's probably a crazy!

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:44.200
Hey, it's starting!

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:48.270
So why are we the Jizo statues?

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:49.390
Is now the time?

00:13:49.630 --> 00:13:53.460
We ended up doing it as a performance.

00:13:53.780 --> 00:13:55.350
I don't like to admit it,

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:58.770
but I invested a lot of my 
personal funds into this set.

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:00.230
Wow!

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:01.950
Cool!

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:04.440
It really looks just like 
the world of a folktale!

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:07.350
Yumoto...

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:10.570
I don't like it.

00:14:12.260 --> 00:14:15.730
Oh! I have failed to sell 
my hats once again today!

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:16.100
Not great!

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:17.750
What a stiff reading!

00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:19.330
Excellent job, Yumoto.

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:20.250
You're doing perfectly.

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:23.240
How awful!

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:25.920
These Jizo statues are covered in snow!

00:14:26.200 --> 00:14:28.130
I have got to help them!

00:14:32.380 --> 00:14:34.060
I am lacking one hat!

00:14:34.330 --> 00:14:35.700
What am I to do?

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:37.100
I know!

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:41.940
So cold!

00:14:43.160 --> 00:14:44.570
I like that old man!

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:46.960
But I think the Jizo is choking...

00:14:46.960 --> 00:14:47.930
Yumoto.

00:14:48.270 --> 00:14:50.610
Your big brother will warm you up later!

00:14:50.870 --> 00:14:51.680
Why?!

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:53.120
Why are they laughing?!

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:55.870
This is supposed to be a moving scene!

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:04.500
<i>Welcome to the VEPP Theater.</i>

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:13.220
<i>VEPPer, the twin stars 
racing through the galaxy!</i>

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:16.470
<i>Let's illuminate the mysteries 
of the universe...</i>

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:20.240
<i>On the name of the stars!</i>

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:37.330
The twin stars shining in the heaven!

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:38.330
Salty Sol!

00:15:38.770 --> 00:15:40.250
Melty Luna!

00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:44.580
Galaxy Idols, the VEPPer!

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:47.050
Chosen warrior!

00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:48.960
Lucky you!

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:50.920
Happy you!

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:53.230
Shooting...

00:15:53.230 --> 00:15:54.840
Star!

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:05.350
I will recite... the folktale!

00:16:05.350 --> 00:16:06.480
Because...

00:16:06.660 --> 00:16:08.960
I want to move the children's souls!

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:12.220
Yes, the one who loves recitation,

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:14.610
and longs to recite...

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:16.980
Mic Monster!

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:18.840
E-E-Everyone!

00:16:18.840 --> 00:16:22.490
A suspicious intruder! Well, 
I'm in no position to judge...

00:16:22.490 --> 00:16:23.260
Seriously?

00:16:23.260 --> 00:16:24.670
At a time like this?

00:16:24.940 --> 00:16:26.380
Why, you...

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:29.510
the kids were feeling 
really moved by the story!

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:34.180
I want to inspire those kids 
the way my brother inspired me!

00:16:34.490 --> 00:16:35.620
Yumoto...

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:37.600
You've grown up so much...

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:40.910
Love Making into the Battle Lovers!

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:45.250
Love Making!

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:50.480
The Sparkling Prince!

00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:53.780
Battle Lover Scarlet!

00:16:54.310 --> 00:16:55.530
The Flashing Prince!

00:16:56.210 --> 00:16:57.740
Battle Lover Cerulean!

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:00.260
The Piercing Prince!

00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:02.580
Battle Lover Epinard!

00:17:04.220 --> 00:17:05.660
The Roaring Prince!

00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:08.040
Battle Lover Sulfur!

00:17:08.870 --> 00:17:10.130
The Thrilling Prince!

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:12.450
Battle Lover Vesta!

00:17:17.740 --> 00:17:21.430
This love-filled planet will 
not abide those who lack love!

00:17:21.660 --> 00:17:25.140
Those who wield loveless 
power must kneel before love!

00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:26.770
Love is power!

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:28.350
Love is hope!

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:29.950
Be born for love!

00:17:29.950 --> 00:17:31.820
Give your life for love!

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:32.980
Love!

00:17:32.980 --> 00:17:35.770
We are, forever, the heirs 
to the throne of love...

00:17:36.080 --> 00:17:37.240
Battle Lovers!

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:39.080
Feel the power...

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:40.960
Of love!

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:45.090
I'm the prince of microphones, Mic Monster!

00:17:45.090 --> 00:17:48.280
Listen! I'll let you hear a true recitation!

00:17:48.280 --> 00:17:51.920
Ladies and gentlemen, watch as I bring 
a moving end to this performance!

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:53.320
Is it a hero show now?

00:17:53.320 --> 00:17:54.670
The blur-faces are funny!

00:17:54.670 --> 00:18:02.940
Once... upon a time... 
off... in the mountains...

00:17:55.460 --> 00:17:56.640
Hey, you!

00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:59.840
If you want to move someone, the skill 
of the performance doesn't matter!

00:18:00.040 --> 00:18:02.940
As long as you're giving it everything 
you have, the feeling will get through!

00:18:02.940 --> 00:18:04.350
Silence, amateur!

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:08.150
I'll show you the power of a true reciter!

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:14.610
Take this! Cry of my soul!

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:15.150
<b>Soul   Cry</b>

00:18:16.480 --> 00:18:18.000
"Soul" hurts!

00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:19.320
Yeah, the kanji does have a lot of strokes!

00:18:19.560 --> 00:18:21.780
"Cry" hurts a lot, too!

00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:24.090
Do you see now?

00:18:24.090 --> 00:18:26.780
My attacks are cries from my soul!

00:18:26.780 --> 00:18:30.000
My words take form and become weapons!

00:18:30.320 --> 00:18:32.000
I don't get it!

00:18:32.240 --> 00:18:34.960
Just watch out for flying kanji!

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:37.590
Next up... all of my resentment!

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:37.590
<b>Resentment</b>

00:18:39.310 --> 00:18:40.840
"Resentment" hurts, too!

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:43.270
And it's heavy, as well!

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:46.900
My set!

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:50.520
I spent a lot of money on that...

00:18:51.140 --> 00:18:53.890
And I threw away my pride to play a Jizo!

00:18:53.890 --> 00:18:55.440
Don't get in our way!

00:18:55.440 --> 00:18:57.080
Shut up!

00:18:57.080 --> 00:18:58.390
I have a dream!

00:18:58.390 --> 00:19:02.050
A dream to make others 
weep at my performance...

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:07.120
<b>Dream</b>

00:19:06.530 --> 00:19:09.210
Come true, my dream!

00:19:12.860 --> 00:19:14.340
"Dream" hurts, too!

00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:16.300
And he's pretty annoying.

00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:17.950
That monster is scary!

00:19:16.450 --> 00:19:19.010
Keep fighting, blurry guys!

00:19:19.240 --> 00:19:20.970
Rise again, Yumoto!

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:22.750
You...

00:19:22.750 --> 00:19:25.060
For whose sake do you speak?!

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:26.180
What?!

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:28.600
Love is something you give to others!

00:19:28.960 --> 00:19:31.310
That's what my brother taught me!

00:19:31.540 --> 00:19:32.960
That's right, Yumoto...

00:19:32.960 --> 00:19:35.270
Give, and it shall be given to you!

00:19:35.690 --> 00:19:37.480
To give is true love!

00:19:37.740 --> 00:19:41.060
My brother's folktales probably 
weren't read all that well!

00:19:41.060 --> 00:19:43.600
But they always moved me!

00:19:43.980 --> 00:19:46.340
Because even though he was 
probably exhausted and sleepy,

00:19:46.340 --> 00:19:48.450
he'd tell them just for me!

00:19:48.860 --> 00:19:52.260
Because my brother's stories 
were full of his love!

00:19:52.260 --> 00:19:53.420
Yumoto.

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:54.920
Sweet dreams.

00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:58.040
What's important isn't the 
skill of the performance!

00:19:58.040 --> 00:19:58.630
It's the love!

00:19:58.800 --> 00:19:59.730
Love!

00:20:01.530 --> 00:20:05.350
Let's go! Scarlet Love Lumiere!

00:20:05.510 --> 00:20:05.800
Love

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:10.680
Love is here!

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:12.120
Now!

00:20:12.120 --> 00:20:14.150
Hit him with our love!

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:17.320
Sparkle, Lumiere of Love!

00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:22.070
Flash, Purifying Aqua!

00:20:22.850 --> 00:20:25.530
Pierce, Gallant Hurricane!

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:28.740
Roar, Raging Gaia!

00:20:29.500 --> 00:20:31.960
Thrill, Blazing Ignit!

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:48.430
True Love Attack!

00:20:57.710 --> 00:21:01.610
True Love Fountain!

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:15.920
Love is over!

00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:17.880
Yeah!

00:21:35.010 --> 00:21:36.100
These are great!

00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:38.100
Tastes like mom's home cooking, huh?

00:21:38.100 --> 00:21:38.980
Yeah.

00:21:42.580 --> 00:21:43.690
Bro,

00:21:43.960 --> 00:21:45.820
this reminded me.

00:21:46.220 --> 00:21:48.910
Even though you were 
always so busy with work,

00:21:49.490 --> 00:21:52.160
you'd say that you were always watching me.

00:21:52.470 --> 00:21:55.140
That you were watching out 
for me, day and night,

00:21:55.140 --> 00:21:57.220
like the moon in the daytime sky.

00:21:59.320 --> 00:22:00.110
Yeah.

00:22:02.240 --> 00:22:04.560
You've grown, Yumoto.

00:22:12.510 --> 00:22:14.220
<b>Curse</b>

00:22:17.410 --> 00:22:20.510
Hakone Yumoto. He's truly in our way.

00:22:20.510 --> 00:22:23.150
Yes. The Defense Club has to go.

00:22:23.450 --> 00:22:25.740
Don't be so impatient, my twins.

00:22:25.740 --> 00:22:28.910
The curtain of battle has only just gone up.

00:24:01.960 --> 00:24:04.450
Next time: The Synchronicity of Love.

00:24:01.960 --> 00:24:05.960
<b>Next time</b>

00:24:01.960 --> 00:24:05.960
The Synchronicity of Love

00:24:04.450 --> 00:24:05.960
Love making!
